A quick Instant Pot casserole that makes a hearty breakfast, brunch, or dinner. Frozen hash brown cubes and savory ham steaks are layered, pressure-cooked in seasoned broth, and topped with a blanket of gooey melted cheese.

*Adapted from [Instant Pot Official Recipes](https://recipes.instantpot.com/recipe/cheesy-ham-and-potato-casserole/).*

## Ingredients

- 1 cup chicken or beef broth
- 2 lbs frozen unseasoned hash brown cubes (southern-style hash browns)
- 2 frozen thin boneless ham steaks (8 oz each)
- 1 ½ teaspoons minced fresh sage (or ½ teaspoon dried sage)
- 1 teaspoon fresh thyme leaves (or ½ teaspoon dried thyme)
- 1 teaspoon onion powder
- ¼ teaspoon cayenne pepper (optional, for gentle warmth)
- 2 cups shredded Swiss or sharp cheddar cheese (8 oz)

## Instructions

1. **Preheat the Broth Base:** Pour 1 cup of broth into the inner cooking insert of your Instant Pot. Engage the **Sauté** function and watch until wisps of steam begin drifting upward (a very gentle warming—do not let it boil off, as the cooker requires this moisture to pressurize). Switch off Sauté.
2. **Layer Potatoes and Ham:** Scatter an even layer of half the frozen hash brown cubes across the bottom of the pot. Tear or slice the frozen ham steaks into palm-sized pieces and distribute them across the potato foundation. Cover the meat with the rest of the potato cubes. Sprinkle the minced sage, fresh thyme, onion powder, and optional cayenne pepper evenly across the top layer.
3. **Lock and Pressure Cook:** Place the lid on the cooker, twisting until locked, and confirm the pressure valve is positioned to **Sealing**. Program **Manual / Pressure Cook** on **HIGH** for 4 minutes, ensuring the Keep Warm feature is turned off.
4. **Quick Steam Release:** Immediately when the timer beeps, turn the valve to perform a rapid steam release. Once the float pin drops indicating pressure has fully dissipated, carefully unlock and lift away the lid.
5. **Melt the Cheesy Blanket:** Scatter the 2 cups of shredded cheese evenly over the steaming casserole. Rest the lid loosely askew on top of the pot for roughly 5 minutes; trapped heat will melt the cheese into a luscious, gooey crust.
6. **Serve:** Spoon hearty portions directly onto dinner plates while warm and bubbly.

## Notes

- **Potato Type:** Unseasoned cubed hash brown potatoes (often labeled "Southern Style Hash Browns") work best because they maintain their distinct cube shape under pressure cooking without turning into mush.
- **Cheese Options:** Swiss cheese lends a nutty, fondue-like flavor, while sharp cheddar or Colby Jack gives a classic casserole profile.
